{"kind":"grammar","lang":"en","entities":{"n1-224":{"renderings":[{"id":"9d03b999366e2b6c","role":"prose","field":"shortExplanation","source":{"source":"hanabira","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"imported","value":"Expresses that something is the best or most desirable course of action; 'nothing better than...'."},{"id":"7c0a7e2b59707d7e","role":"prose","field":"longExplanation","source":{"source":"hanabira","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"imported","value":"The ～に越したことはない grammar point indicates that a certain state or action is the most favorable or ideal. It literally conveys the idea that nothing surpasses the stated condition."},{"id":"348e8cf2377458d5","role":"prose","field":"formation","source":{"source":"hanabira","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"imported","value":"Verb (dictionary form) + に越したことはない, い-Adjective + に越したことはない, な-Adjective/Noun + である + に越したことはない"},{"id":"556f27d93b2e6936","role":"prose","field":"usageNote","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"に越したことはない: it is best to, nothing beats (早いに越したことはない)."},{"id":"6b4d498c02a32dcd","role":"label","field":"family","source":{"source":"gokan","ref":"should"},"match":"id","status":"reviewed","value":"Should (Advice / Expectation)","of":{"kind":"family","id":"should"}}]},"n1-224#56d964f683de":{"renderings":[{"id":"3e4d6239ec550026","role":"translation","source":{"source":"hanabira","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"imported","value":"It's best to prepare early."}]},"n1-224#b635b107b628":{"renderings":[{"id":"9a35c2292714dba4","role":"translation","source":{"source":"hanabira","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"imported","value":"There's nothing better than using fresh ingredients."}]},"n1-224#d7060f29305f":{"renderings":[{"id":"951b9d1a2b85bc6c","role":"translation","source":{"source":"hanabira","ref":"n1-224"},"match":"id","status":"imported","value":"Safe driving is always best."}]},"n1-224#8faac29bcc7c":{"renderings":[{"id":"3c6ef